{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And the priest shall set her, etc.</b> But was it not already stated, ״וְהֶעֱמִידָהּ לִפְנֵי ה׳״? Rather, they would move her from place to place in order to exhaust her so that her mind would be shaken and she would confess (Sotah 8)." "<b>And unbinds.</b> He undoes the braiding of her hair, in order to disgrace her. From here for the daughters of Israel: an uncovered head is a disgrace for them (Ketubot 72b)." "<b>Before YHWH.</b> At the Nicanor Gate — it is the eastern gate of the Courtyard, the way for all who enter (Sotah 7)." "<b>And places on her palms.</b> To exhaust her — perhaps her mind will be shaken and she will confess, and the Holy Name will not be blotted out upon the waters (Sotah 14)." "<b>The bitter.</b> Named for their end — for they are bitter to her (Sotah 20)." "<b>The诅咒-waters.</b> That deprive her of the world — a term like ״סִלּוֹן מַמְאִיר״ (Ezekiel 28). It is untenable to explain 'cursed waters,' for they are holy, and Scripture did not write 'cursed' but rather ' cursing others' — and Onkelos too did not render 'לִיטַיָּא' but 'מְלַטְטַיָּא' — that make a curse visible in her body."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:34.847282640Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}